    "title": "Wisconsin DOJ investigating officer involved death in Marinette County, suspect crashes after fleeing police - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Adam Rosen ,\n2 hours ago\nNIAGARA, Wis. (WFRV) – A crash in Marinette County that blocked off all north and southbound lanes of traffic on U.S. 141 on Wednesday afternoon has led officials to conduct an officer-involved death investigation.\nPolice department in Wisconsin shows damaged squad car hit by drunken driver, shares preventative tips The crash, according to a Department of Justice release , occurred around 1:11 p.m. after a Niagara Police Officer attempted a traffic stop in the city, near the border of Wisconsin and Michigan.\nThe suspect vehicle reportedly sped off, swerving into oncoming traffic in the 1000 block of Main Street before colliding with a commercial vehicle.\nThe individual was given medical aid at the scene; however, they were pronounced dead. Nobody else was injured during the incident.\nHalloween night bar stabbing in Green Bay, man charged with attempted homicide As is standard policy for the department, the involved officer will be placed on administrative leave.\nThe crash caused seven hours of lane blockages, which were cleared around 8:24 p.m. on Wednesday.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WFRV Local 5 - Green Bay, Appleton.",
